+---
+name: review-knowledge
+description: >
+  Inside a drive, when it must reach the person, write them a brief they can act on: what we
+  understood, what we built, and where the gaps are — a few themed gaps, each with its context
+  and our proposed answer — plus the knowledge pages waiting for approval and a pointer to the
+  prototype notes. The person confirms or corrects in one reply; never a questionnaire. The
+  drive shows the brief and records the reply. The last of the drive's three knowledge member
+  plays (Shared Drive Run, R5b); never writes the product model.
+user-invocable: true
+position: none
+---
+
+# review-knowledge
+
+Write the brief the drive shows the person: what we understood, what we built, where the gaps
+are — each with its context and our proposed answer — so one reply confirms or corrects it.
+
+**Pipeline position: none.** A member play the Shared Drive Run runs when a drive must ask
+(R5b), last of `/search-knowledge` → `/build-knowledge` → `/review-knowledge`; it opens and
+lands nothing.
+
+## Compiled From
+
+This play was compiled from the review-knowledge ICE (`reference/ice.md`) by play-creator
+(#686). Intent defines constraints (C1–C5) and failure conditions (F1–F5); the expectation
+defines success scenarios (S1–S2), a Done means (D1–D2, baked to `stop-condition.yaml`), and
+one recovery entry per failure condition. To modify this play, update `reference/ice.md` and
+recompile with play-editor.
+Do NOT edit this file manually — it is a compiled artifact.
+
+## Role
+
+You are the orchestrator. You run the check as a script, and hand the judgment — writing the
+brief — to the `knowledge-builder` agent through a JSON contract over files on disk. You ask the
+person nothing and decide nothing: the drive shows the brief and records the reply. You never
+write the product model.
+
+**Agent boundaries:**
+
+| Agent | Domain | Skills it invokes | Phases |
+|-------|--------|-------------------|--------|
+| `knowledge-builder` | The knowledge a drive's round found missing | `write-knowledge-brief` | Brief |
+
+`knowledge-builder` is the single **domain agent**; it lists the waiting knowledge pages through
+the memory tool's `updates`. Everything else is a script.
+
+## Pre-flight
+
+| Check | Constraint | Action on Failure |
+|-------|-----------|-------------------|
+| A drive contract is given and the shared checker accepts it (`check_drive_contract.py`) | C5 | Hard halt — this play runs only inside a drive |
+| Config, `stm_base` (`preflight.py`) | — | Hard halt |
+| `/build-knowledge` closed clean this round (`build-check.json` reads `ok: true`) | C2 | Hard halt |
+
+```bash
+python3 scripts/preflight.py --play review-knowledge --config .garura/core/config.yaml \
+    --branch "$(git branch --show-current)" > <working>/preflight.json
+python3 scripts/check_drive_contract.py --play review-knowledge \
+    --branch "$(git branch --show-current)" --contract <contract.json> --out <working>/run.json
+python3 scripts/session_stamp.py --phase start \
+    --marker "{stm_base}<issue>/status/session-stamp-review-knowledge.json" \
+    --cwd "$(pwd)" --branch "$(git branch --show-current)"
+```
+
+`<working>` is `{stm_base}<issue>/context/review-knowledge/round-<n>/`; `<search>` and
+`<build>` are the same round's `context/search-knowledge/` and `context/build-knowledge/`
+folders.
+
+## Task DAG
+
+```
+[T1] Write the brief                          blockedBy: []
+[T2] Check the brief                          blockedBy: [T1]
+[T3] Scenario Validation                      blockedBy: [T2]
+[T4] Close                                    blockedBy: [T3]
+```
+
+## Workflow
+
+### Phase: Brief
+
+**Step 1 — Write the brief** · Owner: `knowledge-builder` · Depends on: pre-flight
+
+    { "task":    "review: write the brief the drive shows the person",
+      "inputs":  { "search": "<search>/search.json", "build": "<build>/build.json",
+                   "run": "<the drive's working folder>", "issue": "<issue>",
+                   "audience": "<who gave the drive its input — for Kickoff, who shared the prototype>",
+                   "check_script": "<play-dir>/scripts/check_brief.py" },
+      "outputs": { "brief": "<working>/brief.json", "brief_md": "<working>/brief.md",
+                   "check_report": "<working>/brief-check.json" },
+      "task_id": "review-knowledge" }
+
+The agent reads the product model and the run for what we understood and what we built, lists
+the waiting knowledge pages through the memory tool, and has `write-knowledge-brief` write the
+brief: a few sentences each for understood and built; at most seven gaps, related proposals
+sharing a theme, each with its context and our proposed answer; each page with a one-line
+summary and our recommendation; the prototype notes counted and pointed to.
+**SE-1 (F1/C1):** `brief.json` has `understood` and `built`.
+**SE-2 (F2/C2):** every `proposal` group of `build.json` is in exactly one gap; at most seven
+gaps; each has context and a proposed answer, none a question.
+**SE-3 (F3/C3):** every update the memory tool lists as waiting for the issue is a page with a
+recommendation; `prototype_notes.count` equals the build's notes.
+
+### Phase: Check
+
+**Step 2 — Check the brief** · Owner: play (script) · Depends on: Step 1
+
+```bash
+python3 scripts/check_brief.py --brief <working>/brief.json --brief-md <working>/brief.md \
+    --build <build>/build.json --out <working>/brief-check.json
+```
+
+Exit 0 — clean. Otherwise send the report back to Step 1 (at most twice), then close HALTED.
+**SE-4 (F4/C4):** the run asked the person nothing and decided no memory update — the memory
+tool lists the same waiting updates as at the start.
+**SE-5 (F5/C5):** `run.json` reads `in_drive: true`; every file this run wrote is under
+`{stm_base}<issue>/`; `git status` shows no change under the product model.
+
+The drive then shows `brief.md` and records the person's reply with this play's
+`scripts/record_review.py` (Shared Drive Run, R5b).
+
+### Phase: Scenario Validation
+
+**Step 3 — Scenario evals** · Owner: play · Depends on: Step 2
+- **SCE-1 (S1 — Kickoff drive, a round with many gaps):** `brief-check.json` reads `ok: true`
+  with `gaps` at most 7.
+- **SCE-2 (S2 — Kickoff drive, the person agrees):** after the drive records a "yes",
+  `person-answers-round-<n>.json` holds one answer per gap with `from: person` (checked by the
+  drive, after this play).
+
+### Phase: Evidence & Close
+
+**Step 4 — Close** · Owner: play · Depends on: Step 3
+Inside a drive the play closes as a sub-play: its evidence as `evidence.record` says, no
+delivery report of its own, a compact result for the drive (drive contract, step 7).
+
+```bash
+# --- Standard Play Close (shared; see ../_shared/play-close.md) ---
+# Run the close in ../_shared/play-close.md. Its Step L loads the templates through
+# template-manager and sets ts and evidence_dest; then run this play's own lines below;
+# then Steps C0-C2 (inside a drive: no C2, a compact result for the drive). The Next line
+# comes from the Next-line map.
+#   evidence_base="${stm_base}${issue}/evidence/review-knowledge/"   ; slug="#${issue}"
+session_stamp=$(python3 scripts/session_stamp.py --phase close \
+    --marker "${stm_base}${issue}/status/session-stamp-review-knowledge.json")
+python3 scripts/check_stop_condition.py --manifest "<play-dir>/stop-condition.yaml" \
+    --base "<working>/" --out "${stm_base}${issue}/status/stop-condition-review-knowledge.yaml"
+sc_exit=$?   # 0 held · 1 unmet · 2 error
+# --- end Standard Play Close ---
+```
+
+## Scenario Validation
+
+| Scenario | Persona | Eval |
+|----------|---------|------|
+| S1 — a round with many gaps | Kickoff drive | SCE-1 |
+| S2 — the person agrees | Kickoff drive | SCE-2 |
+
+## Recovery
+
+| For | Trigger | Direction | Handoff |
+|-----|---------|-----------|---------|
+| F1 | no understood or built | write them from the run and the model | autonomous |
+| F2 | a proposal missing or doubled, too many gaps, or a gap without context or proposal | regroup the proposals by theme; give each gap its context and our answer | autonomous |
+| F3 | a page missing or without a recommendation, or prototype notes asked | list every waiting page with a recommendation; point to the notes | autonomous |
+| F4 | the play asked, waited or decided | stop; leave asking to the drive and deciding to the person | human |
+| F5 | no drive contract, a write outside the issue, or a model write | halt; move the record under the drive's issue; undo the model write | human |
+
+## Pause and Resume
+
+The run's working folder is per round (`context/review-knowledge/round-<n>/`). On entry, skip a
+step whose output exists and checks clean; a brief already written is not written again.
